## Data Flow Examples

### Example 1: Multi-Broker Order Placement
```
User (Web) → Engine-C Orchestrator → BrokerFactory
→ Check user settings: broker = "zerodha"
→ ZerodhaAdapter → Zerodha Kite API
→ Order placed → Log to Firestore
→ Return order ID to user
```

### Example 2: Iceberg Order Execution
```
User: Place iceberg order (10,000 RELIANCE shares, 100 visible)
→ Engine-C IcebergOrder class
→ Loop 100 times:
  → Place LIMIT order for 100 shares
  → Wait 2 seconds
  → Repeat
→ Aggregate results → Return avg execution price
```

### Example 3: Iron Condor Strategy
```
User: Execute iron condor on NIFTY (21,500/21,600 CE, 20,500/20,400 PE)
→ Engine-C IronCondorStrategy
→ Place 4 orders simultaneously:
  1. Sell 21,500 CE (collect ₹100 premium)
  2. Buy 21,600 CE (pay ₹50 premium)
  3. Sell 20,500 PE (collect ₹100 premium)
  4. Buy 20,400 PE (pay ₹50 premium)
→ Calculate net credit: ₹100
→ Calculate max profit: ₹100, max loss: ₹900
→ Log to Firestore
```

### Example 4: Portfolio Greeks Calculation
```
User: View portfolio Greeks
→ Engine-A Risk Analyzer → GreeksCalculator
→ Fetch all options positions from Firestore
→ For each position:
  → Calculate Delta, Gamma, Theta, Vega, Rho (Black-Scholes)
  → Weight by quantity
→ Aggregate portfolio Greeks
→ Return: Total Delta = +50 (net long), Total Theta = -₹2,500/day
```

